        {"after": "## 5. Worked examples and applications",
         "md": "**Worked example — why Bt cotton works.** The caterpillar bites the leaf; the plant's own cells now carry the *cry* gene from *Bacillus thuringiensis* and produce an inactive protoxin. The insect's alkaline gut juice dissolves it, the toxin is activated, gut cells rupture and the larva dies within days. Humans and birds have acidic guts — the toxin is inactive for us. One gene moved the pesticide from the spray can into the plant."},
