        {"after": "# Bioremediation, biogas",
         "md": "Microbes can be put to work on our waste. **Bioremediation** uses microorganisms to break pollutants down into harmless substances — oil-eating bacteria (*Pseudomonas*) after spills, microbes cleaning sewage in treatment plants. **Biogas** is the fuel side of the same idea: anaerobic methanogen bacteria digest animal dung and plant waste and release methane-rich gas for cooking and lighting."},
